🐛 Bug
The following code:
def get_overload_annotations(mod):
    # original function => [(mangled overload name, overload function)]
    overloads = {}

    for name in dir(type(mod)):
        item = getattr(mod, name, None)
        if not callable(item):
            continue

Ignores __jit_ignored_attributes. It should respect those and not get those attributes. This can be important because some of those attributes may be @Property attributes which you do not want to call when running torch.jit.script.
To Reproduce
class A(nn.Module):
    __jit_ignored_attributes__ = ["ignored"]
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
    @property
    def ignored(self):
        raise ValueError("shouldn't be called")

torch.jit.script(A()) # will error

Expected behavior
This shouldn't error because the attribute should be ignored.
