at::numeric_limits comes with this warning:



      pytorch/aten/src/ATen/cuda/NumericLimits.cuh


        Lines 22 to 24
      in
      1c34fb4







           // WARNING: the following at::numeric_limits definitions are there only to support 




           //          HIP compilation for the moment. Use std::numeric_limits if you are not 




           //          compiling for ROCm. 





Which is out of date. Following the discussion in #50902 (comment) it seems that ROCm can now handle std:numeric_limits in device code just fine. However, as of #11091, at::numeric_limits has two non-standard functions lower_bound() and upper_bound() so it can't be removed completely.
